+Concise Bounded Description
+--------------------------
+
+Use :meth:`~rdflib.graph.Graph.cbd` to extract the *Concise Bounded
+Description* of a resource: the subgraph that describes it, as defined in the
+W3C member submission at https://www.w3.org/Submission/CBD/.
+
+The description contains:
+
+* every triple whose subject is the resource;
+* for each blank node reached as an object, every triple with that blank node
+  as subject (followed recursively, so cycles are safe);
+* reified statements about the resource (``rdf:Statement`` nodes whose
+  ``rdf:subject`` is the resource), together with their triples.
+
+The result is a new :class:`~rdflib.graph.Graph`; the source graph is not
+changed::
+
+    >>> from rdflib import Graph, URIRef, BNode, Literal
+    >>> from rdflib.namespace import FOAF
+    >>> g = Graph()
+    >>> alice = URIRef("http://example.org/alice")
+    >>> address = BNode()
+    >>> g.add((alice, FOAF.name, Literal("Alice")))
+    >>> g.add((alice, URIRef("http://example.org/address"), address))
+    >>> g.add((address, URIRef("http://example.org/city"), Literal("Oslo")))
+    >>> cbd = g.cbd(alice)
+    >>> len(cbd)
+    3
+
+This is also the building block for SPARQL ``DESCRIBE`` queries.
+
